  "slug": "intestinal-liver-mice-0dd6",
  "summary": "New NAR database releases and fusion/chimeric RNA tools refine reference layers for interpreting cancer transcriptomes and their regulators.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is infrastructure for interpreting cancer transcriptomes, divided between curated reference resources and transcript-structure discovery. On the resource side, LncRNAfunc 2.0 integrates TCGA, GTEx, CCLE, binding and perturbation evidence for regulatory and functional interpretation of cancer lncRNAs. iGPSC-DB catalogs inferred single-cell genetic perturbation effects on tumor phenotypes and microenvironment crosstalk. R-loopBase v2.0 reanalyses 358 R-loop datasets from 16 technologies, adding quantitative confidence scoring and species- and cell type-resolved maps across human, mouse, fly and yeast. On the discovery side, RIFTT combines Arriba and FusionCatcher with new scoring metrics to reduce fusion false positives in tumor RNA-seq, benchmarked on TCGA-LAML and BeatAML. A separate integrative pipeline builds an atlas of 569,640 chimeric RNAs across 1019 cancer cell lines and uses dependency screening to link candidates to cell fitness. TailEnrich, a preprint, tests the tails of expression distributions for disease-sample enrichment to identify genes dysregulated only in patient subsets.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-09"
}
